    "diagramPlacement": "beside-prompt",
    "answer": {
      "short": "Pair the triangle with an identical copy rotated $180^\\circ$. Together they form an $n\\times(n+1)$ rectangle, so the original triangle contains $\\frac{1}{2}n(n+1)$ dots.",
      "worked": "Starting from the bottom, successive rows contain $1,2,3,\\ldots,n$ dots. Pair the triangle with an identical copy rotated $180^\\circ$. Together they form an $n\\times(n+1)$ rectangle containing $n(n+1)$ dots. The original triangle is half of this rectangle, so\n$$1+2+3+\\cdots+n=\\frac{1}{2}n(n+1).$$",
